    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d335">

                <pb facs="0407" n="1141" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1141"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Baron
                            Kettler.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-06-17"><hi rendition="#italic">June 17,
                        1895</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 77.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 13th ultimo, in which you suggest that the decision reached
                    by this Government on the subject of sending their families to join the captive
                    Samoans at Jaluit, as expressed in a letter of the Secretary of State of
                    February 16 last, be reconsidered.</p>
                <p>In reply I beg to say that I shall avail myself of the earliest practicable
                    opportunity to take up the matter, and meanwhile beg to renew to you, sir, the
                    assurances of my high consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
